{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_vrtx_0138RyFEivJTAt1Q5VYNCTDJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. I wrote **`answers/03-021-how-agents-decide-which-tool-to-use.md`** — the answer for Q21: *How agents decide which tool to use?*\n\n**Key content:**\n- **Concept:** LLM function-calling as a semantic match between task context and tool JSON schemas — the model is doing zero-shot classification against tool descriptions.\n- **Mechanism:** Schema injection → ReAct Thought → `tool_call` JSON output → orchestrator allowlist + schema validation → tool execution → Observation injection. Five levers: description distinctiveness, parameter constraints (enums/patterns), T=0, tool retrieval (FAISS/Qdrant cosine top-K) for 15+ tool libraries, and golden-task-set accuracy benchmarking.\n- **Verbal script:** First-person, covers the failure arc of vague/overlapping descriptions (95% → 60% accuracy) and the tool retrieval solution for large libraries.\n- **Pitfalls:** (1) Vague descriptions causing wrong selection; (2) relying on the LLM to self-validate arguments instead of orchestrator JSON schema validation; (3) injecting 30+ schemas every turn without tool retrieval.\n\nNext up: Q22 — *Tool schemas that reduce hallucinated actions?*"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":351,"cache_read_input_tokens":67126,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":351,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"216a8152-360d-44cf-a589-f844cc50a266","uuid":"6c2582ed-871f-4eef-802c-b309a3ded3c5"}
